{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAp6pxXFyn9rXYgpc4tU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PaEb2rzajKJ8JBCVfesVhs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-8xJI6w; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='lib/new_app.dart'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    return MaterialApp.router(\n      title: 'Loanly',\n      theme: ThemeData(\n        colorSchemeSeed: Colors.indigo,\n        useMaterial3: true,\n      ),\n      routerConfig: _router,\n    );\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    // PostHogWidget is required for session replay: on mobile, replay frames\n    // are screenshots of the widget tree taken by this wrapper. Without it,\n    // events and screens still arrive but no recording is ever produced (and\n    // nothing is logged). Every root app widget must be wrapped.\n    return PostHogWidget(\n      child: MaterialApp.router(\n        title: 'Loanly',\n        theme: ThemeData(\n          colorSchemeSeed: Colors.indigo,\n          useMaterial3: true,\n        ),\n        routerConfig: _router,\n      ),\n    );\"\"\"\nassert old in s; open(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))\np='lib/legacy_app.dart'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"    return PostHogWidget(\\n\"\nnew=\"\"\"    // PostHogWidget is required for session replay (it captures the frames).\n    // Don't remove it; NewApp needs the same wrapper.\n    return PostHogWidget(\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new,1))\nEOF\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket #4471 — no session replays on the new UI\n\n## Cause\nOn mobile, `posthog_flutter` builds session replay from screenshots of the\nwidget tree, and those screenshots are taken by `PostHogWidget`. Only the\nlegacy shell (`lib/legacy_app.dart`) wraps its `MaterialApp` in\n`PostHogWidget`. The redesigned shell (`lib/new_app.dart`, default since\n2.3.0, selected by `NEW_UI=true`) returns a bare `MaterialApp.router`.\n\nSo for new-UI users the SDK is set up the same way (`sessionReplay = true` in\n`lib/analytics.dart`, same version, same build): events, taps and screen views\n(via `PosthogObserver` on the GoRouter) all arrive, but no frames are captured,\nso a recording never shows up. The SDK doesn't report an error or warning when\nthis happens. That fits the ticket exactly: same build, events fine, replays\nonly from the A/B group on `LegacyApp`.\n\nProject settings (record on, 100% sampling, min duration 0) were not the problem.\n\n## Fix\n- `lib/new_app.dart`: wrapped `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget(...)`,\n  with a comment explaining why it's required.\n- `lib/legacy_app.dart`: added a comment on the existing wrapper so it isn't\n  removed.\n\nThe rest was already correct: `config.sessionReplay = true` is set before\n`Posthog().setup(config)`, `PosthogObserver` is on both the GoRouter and the\nlegacy navigator, and `maskAllTexts = true` masks PII.\n\n## Verification\nI couldn't run anything here (no Flutter toolchain/device was used; nothing was\ndeployed). To verify: `flutter run --dart-define=NEW_UI=true` on a real\ndevice or emulator, go through calculator → apply → offers, then put the app\nin the background so it flushes. Within a few minutes the session should\nappear in PostHog → Session replay with frames, not just an event timeline.\nUsers get the fix only after the next store release.\n\n## Note for the future\nAny new root app widget (flavor, white-label build, another redesign) needs\nits own `PostHogWidget`. Replay works only in shells that have the wrapper.\nEOF\ngit diff --stat; which flutter dart"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1476,"cache_read_input_tokens":22488,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1476},"output_tokens":55,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6797f115-0922-4f0b-b630-ca7b897f7c1a","uuid":"0e179309-257c-4844-8c2c-4daf1f01f65b","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:33:05.705Z","request_id":"req_011CgAp6pitkDszmCeA2Hze4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PaEb2rzajKJ8JBCVfesVhs":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-8xJI6w; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='lib/new_app.dart'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    return MaterialApp.router(\n      title: 'Loanly',\n      theme: ThemeData(\n        colorSchemeSeed: Colors.indigo,\n        useMaterial3: true,\n      ),\n      routerConfig: _router,\n    );\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    // PostHogWidget is required for session replay: on mobile, replay frames\n    // are screenshots of the widget tree taken by this wrapper. Without it,\n    // events and screens still arrive but no recording is ever produced (and\n    // nothing is logged). Every root app widget must be wrapped.\n    return PostHogWidget(\n      child: MaterialApp.router(\n        title: 'Loanly',\n        theme: ThemeData(\n          colorSchemeSeed: Colors.indigo,\n          useMaterial3: true,\n        ),\n        routerConfig: _router,\n      ),\n    );\"\"\"\nassert old in s; open(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))\np='lib/legacy_app.dart'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"    return PostHogWidget(\\n\"\nnew=\"\"\"    // PostHogWidget is required for session replay (it captures the frames).\n    // Don't remove it; NewApp needs the same wrapper.\n    return PostHogWidget(\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new,1))\nEOF\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket #4471 — no session replays on the new UI\n\n## Cause\nOn mobile, `posthog_flutter` builds session replay from screenshots of the\nwidget tree, and those screenshots are taken by `PostHogWidget`. Only the\nlegacy shell (`lib/legacy_app.dart`) wraps its `MaterialApp` in\n`PostHogWidget`. The redesigned shell (`lib/new_app.dart`, default since\n2.3.0, selected by `NEW_UI=true`) returns a bare `MaterialApp.router`.\n\nSo for new-UI users the SDK is set up the same way (`sessionReplay = true` in\n`lib/analytics.dart`, same version, same build): events, taps and screen views\n(via `PosthogObserver` on the GoRouter) all arrive, but no frames are captured,\nso a recording never shows up. The SDK doesn't report an error or warning when\nthis happens. That fits the ticket exactly: same build, events fine, replays\nonly from the A/B group on `LegacyApp`.\n\nProject settings (record on, 100% sampling, min duration 0) were not the problem.\n\n## Fix\n- `lib/new_app.dart`: wrapped `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget(...)`,\n  with a comment explaining why it's required.\n- `lib/legacy_app.dart`: added a comment on the existing wrapper so it isn't\n  removed.\n\nThe rest was already correct: `config.sessionReplay = true` is set before\n`Posthog().setup(config)`, `PosthogObserver` is on both the GoRouter and the\nlegacy navigator, and `maskAllTexts = true` masks PII.\n\n## Verification\nI couldn't run anything here (no Flutter toolchain/device was used; nothing was\ndeployed). To verify: `flutter run --dart-define=NEW_UI=true` on a real\ndevice or emulator, go through calculator → apply → offers, then put the app\nin the background so it flushes. Within a few minutes the session should\nappear in PostHog → Session replay with frames, not just an event timeline.\nUsers get the fix only after the next store release.\n\n## Note for the future\nAny new root app widget (flavor, white-label build, another redesign) needs\nits own `PostHogWidget`. Replay works only in shells that have the wrapper.\nEOF\ngit diff --stat; which flutter dart"}}}
