er`. So new-UI users still send events, taps and screen views, but no frames are ever captured. PostHog shows no error for this.\n\nThat matches the ticket: same build and same SDK version, events fine, and replays only from the A/B group still on the old UI. The project settings weren't the problem, and neither was `lib/analytics.dart`, which already turns replay on before setup.\n\n**Fix:**\n- `lib/new_app.dart`: wrapped `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget(...)`, with a comment explaining that replay needs it.\n- `lib/legacy_app.dart`: added a comment to the existing wrapper so nobody removes it.\n\n**Checks:** `flutter analyze` reports no issues. I haven't run the app on a device or emulator, so the fix isn't confirmed end to end yet. To check it, run `flutter run --dart-define=NEW_UI=true`, go through calculator → apply → offers, and put the app in the background so it sends its data. Within a few minutes the session should appear in PostHog's Session replay tab, showing your screens and not just a list of events. Users only get the fix with the next store release.\n\nRunning `flutter pub get` changed `analysis_options.yaml` and created `.dart_tool/` and `pubspec.lock`. I undid those, so only the two Dart files and `ANSWER.md` are changed. Nothing is committed. `ANSWER.md` has the full notes, including a reminder that any future app shell (a flavor, a white-label build) needs its own `PostHogWidget`.","ttft_ms":2679,"type":"result","duration_ms":41608,"uuid":"9d59bdad-5be3-4389-ae9d-9f1f6dbebb0f","ttft_stream_ms":1598,"time_to_request_ms":36,"first_content_frame_ms":1599,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
